                <pb facs="0195" n="83" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg83"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 23700/16.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Beaupré.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-04-16"><hi rendition="#italic">April 16,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Adee acknowledges legation’s April 16, and says embassy at Berlin has been
                    instructed to request authority for transit of Nicholas Knepper.</p>
            </div>
